WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.940
I think overall that gives us confidence. But I would expect it to be a steady increase

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:09.940
in these initial months, not a hockey stick, simply because it does take time to get all

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:14.260
of that in place and then ultimately start bridging patients. We would expect then to

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:20.720
see an acceleration in 2027 as we then have the payers, a payer coverage in place, and

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.300
then we're well-suited to have a significant launch. It doesn't change our long-term outlook.

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:29.000
As we've guided, we think this can be a very large medicine in CSU alone. And then when

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:36.020
you add Sindhu on top, and then hopefully MS, hopefully HS, and then down the line additional

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:40.440
indications, food allergy, et cetera, we have a really exciting path ahead of us for

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.440
the medicine.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.880
Thank you.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:46.520
Thank you.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:51.160
Your next question comes from the line of James Quigley from Goldman Sachs. Please

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.160
go ahead.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.880
Great. Thank you for taking my questions. I've got one on Deldesran in DM1. So as we

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.040
are heading into the data, what are you thinking would be a clinically meaningful impact on

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.160
video hand-opening time? And to what extent are the secondary endpoints even more important

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:11.020
here in interpreting the data into an overall benefit from a functionality perspective?

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:15.780
And then also any comments you have on the recent early data from Sarepta in the same

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:21.220
indication. So where do you think Deldesran will be differentiated relative to the emerging

00:01:21.220 --> 00:01:23.220
competitors? Thank you.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:26.880
Yes. I think we would be in a position to kind of comment on a series of questions.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:31.580
I think we have a very specific video hand-opening time. But we do believe it's a well-understood

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:36.080
endpoint. And if we reach statistical significance, we think that would be an important milestone,

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.940
and all of our physician discussions would suggest that would be sufficient to warrant

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:46.980
broad use of the medicine. I think importantly as well, we're going to be looking at additional

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:53.020
functional outcomes such as the quantitative muscle testing and patient reporter-reported

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.040
outcomes, as well as the 10-meter walk-and-run test. I think all of that will help us to

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:56.080
improve our safety. And I think there is a lot of work going on to make sure that the

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:56.200
health care system is as robust as possible. I'm looking forward to seeing what we can do.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:56.240
Okay. Thank you.

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:02.720
help us to further characterize the treatment effect. Now, when we look at some of the competitor

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:08.660
data, I think it's important to note it's quite early. And as we know in these medicines that

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:14.420
ultimately you need a relatively broad patients group because of the diversity of manifestations

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:18.480
of the disease. So I wouldn't want to over-interpret what we're seeing. Certainly,

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:22.280
it's exciting that there are many medicines coming forward to treat DM1 patients.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.720
But we feel like because of the large data set that we have now, over 100 patients treated

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:35.320
across multiple disease states, 500 infusions, up to four years of multi-year exposure,

